 "decisions": [
  {
   "what": "P1 research roster empty: no scout, reference-design, interface or power researcher",
   "why": "trivially powered (5 V in, one LED branch at ~5 mA); a header, an LED, a resistor and a cap need no research",
   "phase": "P1",
   "ts": "2026-10-28T09:26:39"
  },
  {
   "what": "designing under coverage gap: block:B3 led-indicator (no coverage checklist exists for this topology); research not launched",
   "why": "a single LED + series resistor at 4.3 mA from 5 V is textbook; a research pass would build a checklist for a block with no layout risk. Presented at H1 for the person to overrule",
   "phase": "P2",
   "ts": "2026-10-28T09:28:52"
  },
  {
   "what": "D1 KT-0603G (C12624, Extended, Vf 3.1 V listing value); R1 470R (C23179) not 680R",
   "why": "brief asks for an 0603 green LED and there is no Basic one; at Vf 3.1 V 680R gives 2.4-2.8 mA, below the 3 mA floor, 470R gives 3.5-4.6 mA. Vf is the LCSC listing, the datasheet would not download",
   "phase": "P3",
   "ts": "2026-10-28T09:31:06"
  },
  {
   "what": "hand edit: widened the F.CrtYd of C0603, R0603, LED0603-RD from +-0.80x+-0.40 to +-1.40x+-0.70 mm",
   "why": "the EasyEDA courtyards were the body outline and did not enclose the pads (pads reach +-1.15 x +-0.45); IPC courtyard = pads + 0.25 mm, so placement legality and DRC courtyard checks are not lenient",
   "phase": "P3",
   "ts": "2026-10-28T09:32:39"
  },
  {
   "what": "fp_verify and lib_pin_types not run; D1 cathode = pad 1 from symbol K pin + silk chamfer, not datasheet",
   "why": "no IC on the board, so no datasheet extractions to diff against; the KT-0603G datasheet PDF would not download",
   "phase": "P3",
   "ts": "2026-10-28T09:32:40"
  },
  {
   "what": "outline fit 13.05 x 9.08 mm, margin 2.0, corner r 2.0",
   "why": "margin 1.0/1.5 clipped the J1/R1/D1 refdes silk at the edge; 2.0 keeps all silk on the board and stays under the brief's ~15 x 12 mm",
   "phase": "P6",
   "ts": "2026-10-28T09:54:53"
  },
  {
   "what": "parts.json lines now carry refdes and the LCSC attributes",
   "why": "bom_cpl maps ref->LCSC through refdes; without it BOM.csv had no LCSC column (the schematic reviewer's warning 2)",
   "phase": "P9",
   "ts": "2026-10-28T10:07:23"
  },
  {
   "what": "stop at P9: no order, no quote, no board guide",
   "why": "in the Hive ordering at JLCPCB or any purchase is the person's; this is a pipeline test board, not for ordering",
   "phase": "P10",
